          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Consequences for the Region</strong><br>\nThe long-term consequences of the Six-Day War for the region were profound. The territorial changes led to ongoing conflicts and tensions between Israel and its neighbors. Moreover, the Arab world's stance toward Israel and the pursuit of a military solution to the conflict were significantly influenced.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Superpowers and the War</strong><br>\nThe superpowers, particularly the USA and the Soviet Union, played an important role during the war and in its aftermath. While the USA supported Israel, the Soviet Union was more on the side of the Arab states. The superpowers were also involved in efforts to achieve a ceasefire and promote subsequent political solutions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Long-term Impact</strong><br>\nThe long-term impacts of the Six-Day War are still felt today. Israel's territorial gains and the continued occupation of some areas remain central issues in the Israeli-Arab conflict. The war has also permanently shaped the geopolitical landscape of the Middle East and continues to influence relations between the involved states.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
